currentness:
n. The quality of being current; currency; circulation;
   general reception.
n. Easiness of pronunciation; fluency.

mineralizer:
n. An element which is combined with a metal, thus
   forming an ore. Thus, in galena, or lead ore, sulphur is a mineralizer;
   in hematite, oxygen is a mineralizer.

perversions:
n. a curve that reverses the direction of something
n. an aberrant sexual practice; 
n. the action of perverting something (turning it to a wrong use)

reverberatory:
a. Producing reverberation; acting by reverberation;
   reverberative.
n. A reverberatory furnace.
